Short:        Video hardware decode and encode library
Uploader:     (Dale fills this in at upload time)
Author:       Dalsin Limited
Type:         util/libs
Version:      0.1
Requires:     OpenRTG and OpenGPU
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.2.0
Distribution: Aminet

OpenMedia gives Amiga programs a graphics chip's video engines.
openmedia.library decodes and encodes H.264, H.265/HEVC, VP9, AV1 and more
through one interface, with a driver per chip.

Decoded frames go straight into OpenRTG's video RAM, where OpenGPU converts,
scales and composites them, so the CPU never copies a frame.

Drivers: AmigaChrome (the PC's own video hardware through the ACRTG board),
the PiStorm (the Raspberry Pi's VideoCore), and a CPU fallback module built on
FFmpeg for any Amiga. VLC for AmigaOS is its first user.

Status: designed, not built; this readme is ready for the first release.

Licence: MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Dalsin Limited. The FFmpeg fallback module
keeps FFmpeg's LGPL and ships as its own file with its source. If you build on
it, we ask that you credit Dalsin Limited and AmigaChrome.

Source: https://github.com/DalsinAI/openamigamedia
